xreader NEWS -- user-visible change log
========================================

This file tracks user-visible changes.  Internal refactors
(deprecation cleanups, test bootstraps, dev tooling, ...) that
do not change a user-visible behaviour are not listed here;
they are documented in the commit log and in the release
notes generated from debian/changelog at packaging time.

The format is loosely inspired by the GNU NEWS file convention:
one section per released version, newest first.  Each section
opens with a heading like "Changes in 4.7.0" and is followed
by a "Highlights" summary and a bulleted list grouped by
component.

Entries marked with `[SECURITY]` describe a fix for a
vulnerability; see SECURITY.md for the responsible-disclosure
policy.


Changes in 4.8.1 (unreleased -- stabilization gauntlet)
------------------------------------------------------

Highlights:
* **9 backends enabled by default** (pdf, ps, tiff, xps, epub,
  djvu, dvi, comics, pixbuf).  Previously only 5/9 were on by
  default.
* **+6 new stress/leak tests** in tests/test-tabbed-window.c
  (type-registered, 100-tab stress, reorder, reopen-stack bound
  at 10, signal counts, get-by-location).  Test suite now 15
  active C cases.
* **+3 new shims** in libmisc/ev-gtk-compat.h
  (ev_gtk_box_pack_start, ev_gtk_widget_show_all,
  ev_gtk_container_add).  35 call sites across 6 shell/*.c
  files now use the shims, making them dual-target GTK3/GTK4.
* **+1 E2E CI job** (.github/workflows/ci-checks.yml::e2e-python)
  runs the 9 Python Dogtail tests under Xvfb on every PR.
* **Section banners** added to ev-window.c (god object navigation).
* **tools/apply-gtk-compat.py** automates the GTK 3 -> shim
  rewrite for future work.
* **README.md aligned** with the actual 4.8.x state (was
  claiming "tabbed by default" and "GTK 4 ready" both of which
  are not yet true).
* **+1 file removed** (io.github.yuri_schmaltz.Xreader.json,
  the orphaned Flatpak manifest from v4.7.0).

Build, CI, packaging
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Build, CI, packaging
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
* meson_options.txt: djvu, dvi, comics, pixbuf default to true.
* backend/dvi/mdvi-lib/fontmap.c: added missing <glib.h> include
  for g_snprintf under modern toolchains.
* test/meson.build: documented the required: false semantics for
  xvfb-run (Python tests are silently skipped on systems without
  xvfb-run, run in CI where xvfb is installed).

Tests
~~~~~
* New: tests/test-tabbed-window.c (6 cases).
* Existing 14 tests unchanged (test-tab-manager, test-reopen-stack,
  test-tabbed-integration, test-multi-tab-documents, test-ocr,
  test-signatures, test-page-render, test-form-field, test-mime,
  test-rect-intersect, test-session-roundtrip, test-file-helpers,
  test-image, test-document-factory).
* New CI job: e2e-python runs the 9 Python tests under Xvfb
  in addition to the 15 C unit tests.


Changes in 4.8.0-1 (2026-08-28)
---------------------------------

Highlights:
* Optional Multi-Document Tabbed View via EvTabbedWindow (opt-in
  through the `--tabbed`/`-T` CLI flag or the `tabbed-mode`
  GSettings key).  When enabled, a single window hosts multiple
  documents as tabs with per-tab page/zoom/find state and
  middle-truncated tab labels with document icons.
* Keyboard shortcuts for tabs: Ctrl+Tab / Ctrl+Shift+Tab (switch),
  Ctrl+W (close), and Ctrl+Shift+T (reopen last closed tab from
  a LIFO history stack bounded to 10 entries).
* Enterprise X.509 Digital Signature verification engine
  (EvDocumentSignatures) integrated with the Poppler backend.
* Integrated OCR text extraction engine (EvDocumentOCR) powered
  by Tesseract.
* Dual-target GTK build option (`-Dgtk_version=3` or `-Dgtk_version=4`).
* Cross-version GTK compatibility layer (libmisc/ev-gtk-compat.h)
  with shims for box/container/dialog APIs.
* Hardened security gauntlet: DVI TFM font buffer overflows,
  DjVu leaks, EPUB sandboxed permissions (0700), and SyncTeX
  parser bounds checks.
* Single-file Debian package generation tools (tools/build-deb.sh).
* 9 backends enabled by default: pdf, ps, tiff, xps, epub,
  djvu, dvi, comics, pixbuf.


Build, CI, packaging
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

Build, CI, packaging
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `.github/workflows/ci-checks.yml` -- 5 new CI jobs:
  `clang-tidy` (PR #67), `iwyu` (PR #68), `valgrind`
  (PR #69), `coverity-scan` (PR #71, gated on the
  `COVERITY_SCAN_TOKEN` secret), and `clang` (PR #80).
  The total CI count is now 12 jobs.
* `meson.build` -- add `-D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3` (was implicit
  2) and `-fstack-protector-strong` to harden the build
  against stack-based buffer overflows.  (PR #81)
* `tools/release.sh` -- add `--no-push` flag that skips
  the `git push` of master + tag, useful for testing the
  bump+changelog+appdata+commit+tag flow without touching
  the remote.  (PR #84)
* `tools/lint-branches.sh` -- new script (PR #85) that
  enforces the xreader branch-name style (category prefix
  + kebab-case description, max 80 chars).

Public API annotations
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `ev-file-helpers.h` -- add `G_GNUC_PURE` (1) and
  `G_GNUC_MALLOC` (5) on the public helper functions.
  (PR #61)
* `ev-init.c` -- add `G_GNUC_WARN_UNUSED_RESULT` (4) on
  `ev_init` / `ev_is_initialized` / `ev_mutex_trylock`.
  (PR #62)
* `ev-debug.c` / `ev-profile.c` -- add `G_GNUC_PRINTF`
  (3) on the no-varargs stubs of `ev_debug_message` and
  the profiler output functions.  (PR #63)
* 12 `G_GNUC_NONNULL` annotations on the new helper
  functions added in 4.7.0 (PR #43).

gtk-doc blocks
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* 9 headers now have proper `/** ... */` gtk-doc blocks:
  `ev-page.h`, `ev-document-find.h`, `ev-render-context.h`
  (PR #52), `ev-document-annotations.h`,
  `ev-document-attachments.h`, `ev-document-info.h`,
  `ev-document-fonts.h`, `ev-document-images.h`,
  `ev-document-security.h` (PR #56-57),
  `ev-document-forms.h`, `ev-document-layers.h`,
  `ev-document-links.h`, `ev-document-misc.h`,
  `ev-document-print.h`, `ev-document-text.h`,
  `ev-document-transition.h` (PR #58-60).
* `ev-form-field.h` -- add gtk-doc blocks for the
  `ev_form_field_type_to_string` and
  `ev_form_field_type_from_string` helpers added in
  this release.  (PR #78)

API modernization
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `g_slice_*` -> `g_new` / `g_free` in 4 files (10 uses).
  `g_slice_*` was deprecated in glib 2.68; the new API is
  portable across the full glib 2.32+ matrix.  (PR #64)
* `g_get_current_time` + `GTimeVal` -> `g_get_real_time`
  in `ev-file-helpers.c`.  `g_get_current_time` was
  deprecated in glib 2.62.  (PR #65)
* `strcasecmp` -> `g_ascii_strcasecmp` in `ev-document.c`.
  The latter is locale-independent (ASCII-only), which
  is what the document-type dispatch wants.  (PR #66)
* `g_uri_unescape_string` -- add NULL fallbacks in
  `ev-properties-view.c` and `ev-keyring.c` (the
  function returns NULL on malformed URI input).
  (PR #50, #51)

Unit tests
~~~~~~~~~~

* `tests/test-form-field.c` -- 9 new test cases covering
  the form-field type helpers.  Total test count:
  52 -> 61 unit tests.  (PR #79)
* `tests/test-page-render.c` -- 7 test cases for the
  page-render path.  Added in 4.7.0 (PR #60).  Mentioned
  here for completeness.

New helpers
~~~~~~~~~~~

* `libdocument/ev-form-field.c` -- add
  `ev_form_field_type_to_string` and
  `ev_form_field_type_from_string` (PR #78).  Foundation
  for the upcoming B6 PDF form-filling UI.

Build artifacts
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `flatpak/io.github.yuri_schmaltz.Xreader.json` --
  Flatpak manifest for the sandboxed install path.
  (PR #74)
* `snap/snapcraft.yaml` -- Snap manifest for the
  snapd-based install path.  (PR #75)

Data files
~~~~~~~~~~

* `data/xreader.appdata.xml.in` -- expand with
  `bugtracker` URL, screenshots, keywords, and the
  full mimetype list.  (PR #73)

Contributors
~~~~~~~~~~~~

See `debian/changelog` for the full list of contributors.



Changes in 4.7.0 (2026-07-28)
-----------------------

This is the first release since 4.6.5. The 4.7.0 cycle
included 31 self-PRs in the yuri-schmaltz/xreader fork; see
`debian/changelog` for the canonical list.  The
upcoming 4.7.0 release will include the following changes
that were merged into the yuri-schmaltz/xreader fork and are
queued for review in the upstream linuxmint/xreader repository
(track via the PR list in HACKING.md):

Build, CI, packaging
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `debian/control` -- bump `debhelper-compat` from 12 to 13
  and `Standards-Version` from 3.9.6 to 4.6.2; drop the
  `intltool` build dependency in favour of the meson-native
  i18n module; drop the `lsb-release` runtime dependency.
* `.github/workflows/ci-checks.yml` -- new CI workflow
  separate from the distro build, with two jobs: a strict
  `-Werror` build with `-Wall -Wextra -Wformat=2
  -Wformat-security -Wnull-dereference -Wmissing-prototypes
  -Wshadow -Wpointer-arith -Wcast-align -Wstrict-prototypes`,
  and a separate build with `-fsanitize=address,undefined`
  running the test suite under ASan + UBSan.  (PR #8)
* `.github/workflows/ci-checks.yml` -- a third job, a
  60-second libFuzzer smoke run driven by the new
  `fuzz/fuzz-document-load.c` harness.  Crashing inputs are
  uploaded as a `fuzz-crashes` artifact.  (PR #19)

Backend, document parsing
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `backend/epub/` -- migrate the embedded 3,000-line minizip
  fork to the system `libzip` (3,067 lines removed, the
  build now depends on `libzip-dev` instead of compiling
  the fork).  The `.epub` loader API is unchanged.  (PR #12)
* `backend/dvi/mdvi-lib/afmparse.c` -- replace 17
  `malloc(strlen(s)+1) + strcpy` patterns with `g_strdup`,
  add the missing `<glib.h>` include.  (PR #21)

Security
~~~~~~~~

* `[SECURITY]` `libview/ev-print-operation.c`,
  `shell/main.c` -- replace `g_app_info_create_from_commandline`
  with `g_spawn_async` taking an explicit `argv[]` array, so
  that user-controlled arguments from the document (print
  settings, file path) are passed to the child verbatim
  instead of being re-parsed through a shell-style splitter.
  Fixes the third-party report classified as the same
  injection class as the print previewer.  (PR #1)
* `[SECURITY]` `backend/dvi/dvi-document.c` -- replace
  `g_spawn_command_line_sync` (which routes through `/bin/sh
  -c`) with `g_spawn_sync` taking an explicit `argv[]` for
  the `dvipdfm` invocation, so page indices, the
  `exporter_filename`, and the `context->filename` cannot
  inject extra arguments via shell metacharacters.  (PR #2)
* `[SECURITY]` `shell/ev-application.c` `ev_spawn()` --
  same fix as PR #1, but for the `ev_spawn` helper that
  re-launches xreader when the user clicks a link to a
  different document.  The `page-label`, `named-dest`, and
  `--find` arguments can be set by the document, so they
  were all sourced through `g_app_info_create_from_commandline`;
  the new code passes them as a pre-built `argv[]` array.
  (PR #18)
* `[SECURITY]` `backend/dvi/mdvi-lib/paper.c` -- replace
  four `sprintf` calls with `g_snprintf` to bound the write
  to the buffer.  The original code could write up to ~256
  bytes into a stack-allocated 80-byte buffer; the fix
  limits each call to the buffer size and checks the return
  value.  (PR #10)

Modernization
~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* Remove every reference to the deprecated `GTK_STOCK_*`
  macro across `previewer/`, `shell/`, and `libview/`, and
  replace each one with either a localized plain-text label
  (for the cases where the GTK_STOCK_* was used for its
  accelerator underline) or a themed `xsi-*-symbolic` icon
  name (for the cases where the GTK_STOCK_* was used for
  its icon).  The XSI icon names render correctly on HiDPI
  displays and on the modern XApp / Adwaita / Yaru / Papirus
  themes, which no longer ship the legacy full-color names.
  (PRs #3 - #7)
* `libview/ev-stock-icons.c` -- switch the 14 entries in
  the legacy `gtk_icon_factory` registration to their
  matching `xsi-*-symbolic` names, so the `EV_STOCK_*`
  stock ids resolve to modern icons.  (PR #15)
* `shell/ev-window.c`, `previewer/ev-previewer-window.c` --
  switch the `PageSelector` toolbar action's hard-coded
  `text-x-generic` icon to `xsi-text-x-generic-symbolic`.
  (PR #14)

Testing, infrastructure
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `tests/test-file-helpers.c` -- new GLib Testing unit
  tests for the public helpers in `libdocument/ev-file-helpers.h`:
  `ev_mkstemp`, `ev_mkdtemp`, and the zlib compress /
  decompress pair.  Run via `meson test -C build
  test-file-helpers`.  (PR #11)
* `tests/` -- additional unit tests for `ev_mkstemp_file`,
  `ev_file_compress`, `ev_file_uncompress`,
  `ev_xfer_uri_simple`, and `ev_file_get_mime_type`.  Run
  via the same `meson test` driver.  (PR #22)
* `fuzz/fuzz-document-load.c` -- new libFuzzer harness for
  `ev_document_factory_get_document`, covering all 8
  document backends (poppler / djvu / dvi / pixbuf / comics
  / xps / epub / tiff) via the file content sniffer.  Build
  via `-Dfuzz=true` (clang only); the CI fuzz job runs the
  harness for 60 seconds on every PR.  (PR #13)
* `fuzz/corpus/` -- seed corpus for the harness, with
  small samples of each supported document format.
  (PR #23)

Developer experience
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `.editorconfig` -- canonicalize tabs for `*.c` and `*.h`,
  4-space indent elsewhere, UTF-8 + LF, trim trailing
  whitespace except in `.po` catalogs and `.md` prose.
  (PR #16)
* `.gitattributes` -- pin text/binary attributes per file
  extension, set the LF-only line ending rule, register
  diff drivers for `.po`, `.json`, and `.xml`.  (PR #16)
* `.git-blame-ignore-revs` -- empty placeholder file ready
  to be populated with mass-formatting commit SHAs.  (PR #16)
* `SECURITY.md` -- responsible-disclosure policy pointing
  at `security@linuxmint.com`, list of supported versions,
  reminder that public GitHub issues should NOT be used for
  security reports.  (PR #16)
* `.clang-format` -- canonical C source formatter config
  (8-column tabs, GNU control-flow braces, pointers on the
  type, do-not-sort-includes to preserve the existing
  include-block conventions).  (PR #17)
* `HACKING.md` -- developer guide covering build
  prerequisites, the meson build types, the three test
  families, the coding style, and the pull-request flow.
  (PR #17)
* `tools/check-source.sh` -- one-shot source-quality script
  that flags trailing whitespace, accidental tabs in
  non-source files, CRLF line endings, and UTF-8 BOMs, and
  optionally runs `clang-format --dry-run` and `shellcheck`
  on `tools/`.  Intended to be hooked up to a pre-commit
  hook.  (PR #17)
* `tools/lint-commits.sh` -- verify each new commit message
  in `git log origin/master..HEAD` starts with a
  `component: ` prefix and stays under 80 characters per
  line.  (PR #24)
* `RELEASE.md` -- release process: bump version, regenerate
  `debian/changelog`, tag, push, build the deb.  (PR #25)
* `.mailmap` -- canonicalize the 96 distinct author/email
  pairs in the git history down to 78, merging
  `Moser Peter` / `Peter Moser`, `infirit` / `Sander Sweers`,
  `Monsta` / `monsta`, `icarter09` / `Isaac Carter`,
  `raveit65` / `raveit`, `Musa Unal` / `Musa Ünal` /
  `musa` / `m8`, etc.  (PR #20)

Deprecations
~~~~~~~~~~~~

* `shell/ev-password-view.c`,
  `shell/ev-properties-dialog.c` -- remove the deprecated
  `gtk_dialog_get_action_area` calls (deprecated since GTK
  3.12, removed in GTK 4).  The two dialogs already use
  `gtk_dialog_add_button` for the OK / Cancel buttons, so
  the action area was just being read for its border-width
  and box-spacing properties, which we now apply to the
  content area instead.  (PR #26)
